$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis via HWE-olefination: To a solution
of triethylphosphonoacetate (1.68 g, 7.50 mmol) in dry and degassed THF
(20 mL) was added NaH (300 mg, 7.50 mmol, 60 wt-% dispersion in mineral
oil). The mixture was heated to reflux for 0.5 h and then cooled to 0°C.
A solution of 3a (811 mg, 5.00 mmol) in THF (5 mL) was added, and the
mixture was heated to reflux for 1 h, then cooled to ambient temperature
and carefully acidified with HCl (aq., 1 M). The mixture was extracted
with MTBE (3 times, 50 mL each), the combined organic extracts were dried
with MgSO4, filtered and evaporated in vacuo. The residue was purified by
column chromatography in silica using hexane-MTBE mixtures as eluent. 8a
(1.02 g, 4.40 mmol, 88%). Colourless oil. Ethyl
(E)-3-(2-(allyloxy)-4-methoxyphenyl)acrylate (8c). 4 The title compound
was synthesized via HWE-olefination in analogy to 8a. Following the
procedure given above, 3c (747 mg, 3.87 mmol) was converted to 8c (954
mg, 3.64 mmol, 94%). Colourless oil. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.95 (d, J
= 16.1 Hz, 1H), 7.44 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 1H), 6.49 (dd, J = 8.6, 2.3 Hz, 1H),
6.43 (d, J = 2.3 Hz, 1H), 6.42 (d, J = 16.1 Hz, 1H), 6.07 (ddt, J = 17.1,
10.5, 5.2 Hz, 1H), 5.43 (dm, J = 17.3 Hz, 1H), 5.31 (dm, J = 10.5 Hz,
1H), 4.59 (d, J = 5.2 Hz, 2H), 4.24 (q, J = 7.1 Hz, 2H), 3.81 (s, 3H),
1.32 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 168.0, 162.6, 158.8,
139.9, 132.9, 130.3, 118.0, 117.0, 116.3, 105.7, 99.7, 69.3, 60.2, 55.5,
14.5; IR (ATR) ν 1703 (m), 1603 (s), 1259 (m), 1159 (s), 1036 (m); HRMS
(EI) calcd. for C15H18O4 [M+] 262.1205, found 262.1201.
