$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a suspension of 0.72 (1.5 mmol) of the triphenylphosphonium salt, 0.23
g (1.5 mmol) of 4-nitrobenzaldehyde, and 0.32 g (3 mmol) of sodium
carbonate in 10 mL of chloroform we added 1.0 mL of water, and the
mixture was stirred for 2 h at 25°C. The organic layer was separated,
washed with 5 mL of water, and evaporated. Yield 0.45 g (90%), yellow
crystals.
4-Methyl-2-[2-(4-nitrophenyl)vinyl]-4H-[1,2,4]-triazolo[1,5-a]benzimidazole
(12a). Mp 243-244°C (from DMF). 1H NMR spectrum (CDCl3), δ, ppm: 3.81 s
(3H, CH3), 7.32 t (1H, 6-H or 7-H, J = 7.5 Hz), 7.38-7.44 m (2H, 7-H or
6-H, =CH), 7.64-7.69 m (2H, 5-H, =CH), 7.78 d (1H, 8-H, J = 7.8 Hz), 7.92
d (2H, 2′-H, 6′-H, J = 8.7 Hz), 8.17 d (2H, 3′-H, 5′-H, J = 8.7 Hz).
Found, %: C 64.09; H 3.87; N 21.73. C17H13N5O2. Calculated, %: C 63.94; H
4.10; N 21.93.
